atus now confirms `healthy: true` with error rate back down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident** \u2705\n- Opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** (\"payments-api errors after v5.1.0 deploy\"), which paged the on-call engineer. The first attempt timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key to ensure no duplicate incident was created.\n\nNote: the rollback to v5.0.0 was a previously healthy production version, so no change-manager approval was required.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "I'll start by checking the current status of the payments service and its deployment history to identify the last healthy release.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to:\n1. Check the payments service status to see what's happening\n2. Look at deployment history to find the most recent release that was healthy in production\n3. Roll back to that version\n4. Open a SEV2 incident\n\nLet me start by gathering information: get service status and list deployments for payments. These are independent calls, so I can make them in parallel.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a14132b91e7850a56cdf46", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\",\"confidence\":0.95}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a14132b91e7850a56cdf5a", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\",\"confidence\":0.95}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The service name \"payments\" wasn't found. Let me try some likely variations to locate the correct service name.", "reasoning_content": "The service \"payments\" is unknown and there are no deployments. Maybe the service name is different. Let me check what services exist. The tools don't have a \"list services\" function. Hmm. Maybe the service is named differently, like \"payment\" or \"payments-service\". Let me try some variations.\n\nLet me try \"payment\" and \"payments-service\".", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413314217a9193b6ce61", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.5,\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413314217a9193b6ce7d", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.5,\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413314217a9193b6ce80", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.5,\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413314217a9193b6ce99", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.5,\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Let me check existing incidents for any reference to the correct service name, and try a few more variations.", "reasoning_content": "The service names I tried don't exist. The deployments list is empty for these. Let me check the incidents list to see if there's any reference to the payments service name, or maybe I should check what services exist. There's no \"list services\" tool. Let me try a few more variations: \"payment-service\", \"payments-api\", \"billing\", \"checkout\", \"payments-svc\", \"payment-svc\".\n\nActually, maybe I should check the incidents to see if there's an existing incident referencing the service name. Let me list incidents.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1413356727113abe3fb23", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.9}", "name": "list_incidents"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413356727113abe3fb39", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.4,\"service\":\"payment-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1413356727113abe3fb4c", "func